  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 124 PM MDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nThe upper low off the west coast of the northern Baja Peninsula\nwill slowly fill and eject northeastward on Sunday and Sunday\nnight. Pacific moisture will advect into NM ahead of the system\nallowing for scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms to\ndevelop across western NM as soon as Sunday morning. What is left\nof the system will cross the Four Corners on Monday, and scattered\nshowers and isolated thunderstorms should spread eastward to at \nleast the Central Mtn Chain. Precipitation amounts will be light\nboth Sunday and Monday. \n\nAll eyes will then be on an upper level low diving southward along\nthe west coast and the continued moisture advection into NM ahead\nof it. Precipitation coverage should gradually increase Tuesday\nand Wednesday, but precipitation coverage is currently expected to\nbe greatest on Thursday and potentially through Friday as the \nsystem shifts eastward and large scale ascent increases over NM. \nPWATs will increase from around 0.6-0.75\" on Sun/Mon to 0.8-1.0 by\nThu. Snow levels will be high, thus snow is expected only for the\nhighest peaks. Rain showers and isolated thunderstorms will be\ncommon elsewhere.",
